    {
      "number": 805,
      "title": "provider_auth: fall back to Doppler for OAuth client credentials",
      "body": "## Usage\n\n```bash\n# Asana OAuth now works with just Doppler configured — no env exports needed\ndoppler run -- lf op pm ...\n```\n\nOAuth client credentials (Asana and any PM provider) now resolve from the environment first, then fall back to fetching from Doppler when the env vars are unset. Previously, missing `ASANA_CLIENT_ID`/`ASANA_CLIENT_SECRET` (or the equivalent PM provider vars) failed hard with a `CommandUnavailable` error; now the broker shells out to `doppler secrets get <NAME> --plain` before giving up. The error message when both sources miss now mentions Doppler as an option.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `oauth_client_credentials` is now async and threads a Doppler fetch through `read_oauth_client_credential`, which tries env then the secret runner.\n- New `fetch_doppler_secret` runs `doppler secrets get --plain`; the value is consumed inline and never printed.\n- Callers (`start_auth`, `complete_auth`, `refresh_pm_oauth_token`, `oauth_app`) updated to await the now-async credential lookup.\n- Extracted `read_nonempty_value` shared by env and Doppler paths.\n- Tests inject a fake Doppler runner via `oauth_client_credentials_with_doppler_runner` and cover env-preferred, Doppler-fallback, and both-missing cases, with an `EnvGuard`/`env_lock` to serialize env mutation.",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 205,
      "deletions": 20,
      "changed_files": 2
    },
    {
      "number": 806,
      "title": "wave: link concerto to asana, retire root/mobile/workflows waves",
      "body": "## What changed\n\nWires the Concerto wave into Asana PM sync and retires three waves whose roles have been absorbed elsewhere.\n\n```diff\n wave/concerto/GOAL.md  |  3 +++\n wave/mobile/GOAL.md    | 16 ---\n wave/root/*            | 122 ---\n wave/workflows/GOAL.md | 24 ---\n```\n\n## Summary\n\nConcerto's `GOAL.md` gains a `pm` block pointing at its Asana project, so its loop can sync against the same PM backend the other active waves use. The `root`, `mobile`, and `workflows` waves are deleted — `root` was the conductor/garden wave, `mobile` was already archived and dormant, and `workflows` owned the engine machinery. Removing their `GOAL.md`/`README`/`backlog`/`yaml` files trims the wave map down to the waves that are actually looping, keeping scope legible and free of stale ownership claims.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `wave/concerto/GOAL.md`: add `pm.provider: asana` + `asana_project` id\n- Delete `wave/root/` (GOAL.md, README.md, backlog.md, root.yaml)\n- Delete `wave/mobile/GOAL.md` (archived, no active surface)\n- Delete `wave/workflows/GOAL.md`",
      "files": [],
      "additions": 3,
      "deletions": 162,
      "changed_files": 7
    },
    {
      "number": 807,
      "title": "wave: retire the website wave wrapper",
      "body": "## Summary\n\nRemoves the Website wave's steering files (`wave/website/GOAL.md` and `wave/website/MEMORY.md`), retiring the wave wrapper. This follows the earlier retirement of the root/mobile/workflows waves and the linking of concerto to asana — the website wave's orchestration harness is no longer needed to keep the public docs and site in lockstep with the library.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Delete `wave/website/GOAL.md` — the ship-roadmap loop prompt and metrics for truing-up the public site\n- Delete `wave/website/MEMORY.md` — the wave's shipped/model/next memory (site import, one-docs-source, fly.io deploy)\n\nNet: 43 lines removed, no product code touched.",
